WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.980
Episode 56

00:00.000 --> 00:02.980
At the Port in the Sky (Part 2)

00:08.320 --> 00:09.580
<i>No one's here.</i>

00:10.550 --> 00:11.780
Impossible.

00:11.780 --> 00:13.360
Where are you hiding?

00:21.190 --> 00:23.490
<i>She's not in the hallway, either.</i>

00:23.490 --> 00:25.040
<i>Where's the intruder?</i>

00:25.710 --> 00:26.720
<i>Hold on...</i>

00:27.160 --> 00:31.040
<i>The only evidence of an intruder 
was a flash and a shutter sound.</i>

00:31.870 --> 00:34.470
<i>Is there really an intruder here?</i>

00:34.470 --> 00:37.040
<i>Or is this one of the 
Detective Agency's tactics?</i>

00:38.660 --> 00:42.360
<i>They may have set up strobe lights 
all throughout the airport,</i>

00:42.360 --> 00:44.110
<i>on a timer to flash all at once.</i>

00:44.110 --> 00:49.200
<i>If I panic and destroy the room,
they will discover Bram's location.</i>

00:49.200 --> 00:53.070
<i>No, they shouldn't have had 
enough time to prepare all that.</i>

00:54.070 --> 00:55.450
<i>That said...</i>

00:57.920 --> 01:00.410
<i>That brat could pull it off.</i>

01:03.930 --> 01:06.940
<i>This is BAA Flight 801.</i>

01:06.940 --> 01:08.730
<i>Currently flying at an 
altitude of 1,200 feet.</i>

01:08.730 --> 01:12.240
<i>Requesting permission 
to land at Runway 122R.</i>

01:12.810 --> 01:14.620
<i>This is 122R.</i>

01:14.620 --> 01:16.250
<i>You are clear for landing.</i>

01:17.530 --> 01:19.520
I've never had such a mission.

01:20.220 --> 01:21.400
Senpai.

01:22.390 --> 01:26.360
On a date with a weapon 
more deadly than a nuke...

01:26.360 --> 01:30.100
Our job's literally to save the world, huh?

01:26.560 --> 01:33.110
<b>British
Intelligence
Agency Special
Escort Unit</b>

01:27.690 --> 01:33.110
<b>Mission:
Secret Delivery</b>

01:30.100 --> 01:31.340
Yeah.

01:31.340 --> 01:36.440
If we botch this delivery, the world will fall 
into a dark abyss from which there is no escape.

01:37.200 --> 01:41.710
Rampo-san, do we really stand a chance 
against a European military escort?

01:41.710 --> 01:43.280
Obviously.

01:43.280 --> 01:44.990
Who do you think I am?

01:44.990 --> 01:48.880
But their military escorts 
are probably Gifted.

01:48.880 --> 01:50.290
Powerful ones, at that.

01:50.800 --> 01:54.410
If they deliver the the One Order
 to Fukuchi, it's all over.

01:54.410 --> 01:59.350
How many hours... How many days is it going 
to take just to obstruct the delivery?

02:01.900 --> 02:02.900
One second.

02:04.080 --> 02:08.010
Intercepting the European military escort 
will be easier than a kid's errand.

02:08.580 --> 02:10.250
Wanna know why?

02:10.670 --> 02:13.220
Basically, we just need them to think...

02:13.870 --> 02:18.170
"Delivery is too risky. We need to retreat."

02:18.170 --> 02:19.210
That's true.

02:19.630 --> 02:21.110
But how?

02:21.110 --> 02:22.780
Have you forgotten?

02:23.130 --> 02:24.990
We're terrorists.

02:28.770 --> 02:30.580
<i>Explosions at the airport?</i>

02:30.920 --> 02:33.400
Tetchou, Teruko-kun, can you hear me?

02:33.400 --> 02:35.530
Give me a report on those explosions.

02:37.240 --> 02:38.590
Radio jamming!

02:39.300 --> 02:42.220
<i>This is most definitely the 
Detective Agency's doing.</i>

02:43.060 --> 02:44.230
<i>What do I do?</i>

02:44.610 --> 02:47.300
There's one certainty...

02:47.300 --> 02:49.690
That explosion is a <i>very</i> bad development.

02:49.690 --> 02:51.820
I won't be able to get what I need!

02:52.520 --> 02:54.120
I must do something.

02:57.920 --> 02:59.450
Mission complete.

02:59.450 --> 03:03.140
As per your plan,
I've blown up the fuel truck.

03:03.140 --> 03:03.980
<i>Understood.</i>

03:05.630 --> 03:09.130
Now, without a doubt, 
the European military escorts

03:09.570 --> 03:14.930
will determine that there are terrorists 
at the airport who may steal the One Order.

03:16.020 --> 03:21.380
Unlike Fukuchi, Europe has no reason that the
 delivery absolutely must be completed today.

03:21.910 --> 03:23.460
So, naturally...

03:25.500 --> 03:27.920
Explosion and blast detected at the airport!

03:27.920 --> 03:28.810
What?!

03:28.810 --> 03:29.900
What does ground control say?

03:29.900 --> 03:31.710
Communications blocked on all frequencies!

03:31.710 --> 03:32.860
Must be radio jamming!

03:33.180 --> 03:34.810
It's the terrorists!

03:34.810 --> 03:36.480
They know about the delivery!

03:38.510 --> 03:39.520
What do we do?

03:40.500 --> 03:41.980
Abort the delivery mission!

03:42.380 --> 03:43.400
Retreat!

03:55.980 --> 03:57.250
<i>That was close...</i>

03:57.250 --> 03:58.820
<i>I'm saved.</i>

03:58.820 --> 04:00.250
So...

04:00.920 --> 04:04.850
Who disturbs my slumber?

04:06.420 --> 04:11.880
Depending on your answer,
 I may have you pay for that sin in blood.

04:13.060 --> 04:18.740
And now, Fukuchi's stuck at the airport, 
without the One Order.

04:18.740 --> 04:23.070
With no choice but to fend off our attacks,

04:23.070 --> 04:26.160
how long do you suppose 
he can protect Bram?

04:28.330 --> 04:32.350
<i>This is the first time 
I've seen Rampo-san like this.</i>

04:33.490 --> 04:36.890
<i>No enemy can best my intellect.</i>

04:38.030 --> 04:44.630
<i>But if I had to name one enemy who could 
fight back against me, it would be...</i>

04:46.860 --> 04:48.280
What the...

04:48.280 --> 04:49.630
An oil leak?

04:55.570 --> 04:57.140
<i>Was I poisoned?</i>

04:57.440 --> 04:59.450
<i>Was it in the coffee I just had?</i>

04:59.780 --> 05:01.650
<i>Who would have done this?</i>

05:05.200 --> 05:06.910
<i>I'm losing consciousness...</i>

05:07.430 --> 05:09.890
<i>The plane's going to crash!</i>

05:10.830 --> 05:12.950
Senpai! You have to take over!

05:14.860 --> 05:16.030
Please, no...

05:16.400 --> 05:19.030
<i>Flight 801, you are off course.</i>

05:19.030 --> 05:21.500
<i>Restore your altitude and resume landing.</i>

05:21.500 --> 05:23.250
<i>You are headed into a restricted area!</i>

05:24.500 --> 05:25.420
This is bad.

05:29.770 --> 05:32.310
Crashing into the airport...

05:32.310 --> 05:34.150
Just as Captain Fukuchi had predicted.

05:38.090 --> 05:40.290
Slash 'em up, Tetchou!

05:42.780 --> 05:46.280
<b>Evil, begone</b>

05:43.770 --> 05:45.520
Evil, begone.

05:48.120 --> 05:50.500
Plum Blossoms in the Snow!

06:00.930 --> 06:02.180
That was a hit.

06:15.070 --> 06:16.140
Captain!

06:17.260 --> 06:19.000
Rampo-san, can you hear me?

06:19.000 --> 06:20.570
The situation could not be worse.

06:20.920 --> 06:23.130
The plane was hurtling toward the airport.

06:23.130 --> 06:24.820
The Hunting Dogs tore it apart...

06:25.380 --> 06:29.520
and Fukuchi retrieved the 
One Order from the wreckage.

06:30.660 --> 06:32.030
In other words...

06:32.940 --> 06:34.650
<i>We've lost.</i>

06:35.460 --> 06:37.100
<i>What do we do, Rampo-san?</i>

06:37.100 --> 06:38.340
<i>What's our next move?</i>

06:39.270 --> 06:40.230
<i>Hello?</i>

06:40.580 --> 06:41.650
<i>Hello, Rampo-san?</i>

06:41.980 --> 06:43.050
<i>Do you hear me?</i>

06:43.810 --> 06:50.480
<i>Like a thunder strike on a summer evening, 
it struck me what we were up against.</i>

06:51.690 --> 06:53.170
<i>That man...</i>

06:53.170 --> 06:56.770
<i>The demon who controls 
the surface from the underground...</i>

06:57.520 --> 07:00.960
<i>Our defeat approached because 
we were unable to eliminate him.</i>

07:01.870 --> 07:03.120
<i>Even now...</i>

07:03.880 --> 07:05.850
<i>If we'd made just one more mistake,</i>

07:05.850 --> 07:08.390
<i>we would have lost the One Order.</i>

07:11.650 --> 07:12.610
<i>It won't open!</i>

07:13.080 --> 07:16.920
<i>This box is shrouded in a 
dimensional disruption ability.</i>

07:16.920 --> 07:19.500
<i>It's impossible to open by physical means.</i>

07:19.820 --> 07:23.190
<i>I can't get to the One Order!</i>

07:23.190 --> 07:24.080
<i>Why?</i>

07:24.830 --> 07:27.400
<i>Who the hell did this?!</i>

09:04.850 --> 09:08.650
<b>Eleven
 hours ago</b>

09:06.660 --> 09:08.650
Thank you for your understanding.

09:08.650 --> 09:11.190
<i>The United Nations is an ivory tower.</i>

09:11.190 --> 09:13.310
<i>It may be that no amount 
of official persuasion</i>

09:13.310 --> 09:16.070
<i>will convince them that you aren't lying.</i>

09:16.070 --> 09:18.670
<i>What of the rumor that Fukuchi 
is behind the vampire pandemic</i>

09:18.670 --> 09:21.980
<i>and that he mustn't be given the One Order?</i>

09:21.980 --> 09:24.950
They don't need to reconsider.

09:24.950 --> 09:28.890
I simply ask for a modicum of caution.

09:29.510 --> 09:31.960
This is my proposal to the United Nations:

09:31.960 --> 09:34.210
In order to prevent a worst-case scenario,

09:34.210 --> 09:41.930
the One Order should only be unlocked
 when the vampirized forces attack.

09:42.230 --> 09:47.270
<i>You suggest delaying until the trumpets
 of the final judgment are heard.</i>

09:47.270 --> 09:50.020
I'm sure Europe is furious, as well.

09:50.020 --> 09:54.850
A hero he may be, but to hand the One Order 
to a soldier from another nation...

09:57.310 --> 09:58.560
<i>Very well.</i>

09:58.560 --> 10:00.520
<i>But I want to be clear</i>

10:00.520 --> 10:05.700
<i>that this plan was determined by Chief Taneda 
and the Gifted Special Operations Division.</i>

10:05.700 --> 10:07.690
<i>Is that correct?</i>

10:14.760 --> 10:17.080
Don't worry, Ango.

10:19.020 --> 10:21.300
The time is ripe for a lie.

10:23.020 --> 10:23.990
Yes.

10:23.990 --> 10:25.700
Chief Taneda has already woken up.

10:25.700 --> 10:27.310
He is in command.

10:27.310 --> 10:29.240
This was his order, as well.

10:29.750 --> 10:31.040
<i>All right.</i>

10:31.040 --> 10:32.780
<i>Stand by for further orders.</i>

10:33.370 --> 10:35.920
Thank you, Prime Minister.

10:43.070 --> 10:46.270
Now, if the chief doesn't wake up,
 I'll be dismissed.

10:47.040 --> 10:47.990
Worse...

10:47.990 --> 10:49.590
I'll be a political criminal.

10:52.840 --> 10:54.240
I bet you're laughing about now,

10:54.830 --> 10:56.270
you nasty man.

10:57.660 --> 11:01.470
Thankfully, Dazai's insurance 
policy paid off.

11:01.470 --> 11:05.500
But it's still the case that the 
One Order was stolen in its box.

11:06.200 --> 11:08.520
Fyodor is still too dangerous.

11:12.700 --> 11:14.280
Warning! Warning!

11:14.600 --> 11:17.120
<i>Intruder in the Level One Delivery Bay!</i>

11:17.490 --> 11:20.850
<i>Anti-Gifted Fast Response Squad 
Hecatoncheires has been eliminated!</i>

11:20.850 --> 11:24.130
<i>All security personnel to 
combat stations immediately!</i>

11:25.800 --> 11:28.820
I'm bored of this room now.

11:29.180 --> 11:31.450
It was fun at first...

11:31.450 --> 11:34.350
But we're out of stuff 
to talk about now, too.

11:34.600 --> 11:36.580
Maybe it's time to do the thing.

11:36.580 --> 11:37.830
The thing?

11:40.850 --> 11:42.810
One of us dies.

11:48.210 --> 11:50.310
That is a fantastic idea.

11:50.310 --> 11:51.780
Right?!

11:51.780 --> 11:54.640
The surface is abuzz about 
the end of the world.

11:54.640 --> 11:57.730
If the two of us end up being 
the last ones alive...

11:58.080 --> 11:59.400
It'd be stupid.

11:59.400 --> 12:01.450
I absolutely agree.

12:01.450 --> 12:02.950
Then maybe it's time to escape—

12:04.540 --> 12:05.750
Fyodor?

12:05.750 --> 12:08.560
Don't you think you're 
jumping the gun just a little—

12:16.060 --> 12:18.880
Breakout magic successful!

12:18.880 --> 12:20.810
Just as suspected!

12:20.810 --> 12:25.310
Dazai-kun's ability only disables 
any special ability he <i>touches!</i>

12:25.310 --> 12:27.330
In other words...

12:27.330 --> 12:29.160
As long as he doesn't 
touch the portal itself,

12:29.160 --> 12:31.580
I can still pull him 
through spatial splices!

12:31.920 --> 12:34.730
Applause for my assistant!

12:34.730 --> 12:35.780
Who are you calling your assistant?

12:35.780 --> 12:38.860
Shouldn't you be telling 
them what's going on?

12:38.860 --> 12:41.120
No worries, no worries.

12:41.120 --> 12:42.820
I see.

12:42.820 --> 12:44.310
So that's what's going on.

12:44.640 --> 12:45.980
Told you.

12:45.980 --> 12:48.070
They get it already.

12:48.340 --> 12:51.570
Why did you break us out of our cells?

12:52.400 --> 12:54.500
I missed you, bestie!

12:54.790 --> 12:57.870
I'm so glad you're safe, 
my heart's going to burst!

12:58.320 --> 13:02.200
Why am I here? Do you even need to ask?

13:02.630 --> 13:04.840
I'm here to murder you.

13:07.520 --> 13:08.430
Wow.

13:09.380 --> 13:13.830
The desire to save one's friend is strong.

13:13.830 --> 13:16.390
Thus, I will overcome it 
with unwavering resolve.

13:16.700 --> 13:19.350
That is a true display of human free will!

13:19.350 --> 13:22.110
You have some awesome friends.

13:21.380 --> 13:23.390
Alas, alas, alas!

13:23.390 --> 13:26.260
Therein lies a philosophical conundrum!

13:26.260 --> 13:32.350
To kill Fyodor now would only be fulfilling
an impulse to prove my own free will.

13:32.860 --> 13:36.560
Might that only be further evidence 
of an animalistic emotion?!

13:37.190 --> 13:40.280
Having contemplated this 
mind-rending problem,

13:40.280 --> 13:42.720
I've finally arrived at a conclusion!

13:42.720 --> 13:46.890
I've arrived at a plan to 
satisfy both of these desires!

13:47.290 --> 13:52.260
I'll have the two of you 
conduct a prison break!

13:55.130 --> 13:58.700
You <i>really</i> have some awesome friends.

13:58.700 --> 13:59.970
Right?

14:01.330 --> 14:05.900
You, who interrupts my slumber. 
Who are you?

14:05.900 --> 14:09.490
Depending on your answer, 
I may not spare you.

14:09.780 --> 14:12.000
I, er... I'm...

14:12.000 --> 14:13.670
I cannot hear you.

14:14.580 --> 14:16.970
Who do you think I am?

14:16.970 --> 14:21.450
Know that I am the master of darkness.

14:22.000 --> 14:27.270
Your life is naught but the fleeting morn dew
in the moments before cockcrow.

14:27.270 --> 14:28.520
Understand?

14:29.070 --> 14:31.670
No. I have no idea what you just said.

14:31.670 --> 14:33.090
What's a cockcrow?

14:33.090 --> 14:36.710
Basically, I am the lord and the storm.

14:36.710 --> 14:38.580
The heavens and the hells.

14:38.580 --> 14:40.150
Wherefore...

14:41.210 --> 14:43.920
I suddenly don't care anymore.

14:44.370 --> 14:45.280
G'night.

14:47.330 --> 14:48.660
Wait...

14:49.480 --> 14:51.370
Why do you look like that?

14:51.780 --> 14:54.570
You've got no body from the neck down.

14:54.820 --> 14:57.340
How do you wash your face in the morning?

14:57.340 --> 14:58.420
I do not.

14:58.420 --> 14:59.450
Gross.

14:59.840 --> 15:02.850
You're so different from
 how you seemed at first.

15:02.850 --> 15:05.920
Aren't you with that scary 
old guy with the katana?

15:06.720 --> 15:07.930
On the contrary.

15:08.330 --> 15:10.520
Fukuchi is my shackle.

15:10.520 --> 15:13.130
My arch-nemesis who impaled 
me upon this holy sword

15:13.130 --> 15:15.860
and took from me the 
ability to control my kin.

15:15.860 --> 15:17.390
Arch-nemesis?

15:19.410 --> 15:20.760
What's your name?

15:20.760 --> 15:22.390
Count Bram.

15:22.390 --> 15:24.100
I'll just call you Bra-chan, then.

15:24.100 --> 15:25.090
Bra-chan?

15:25.430 --> 15:27.900
Hey, Bra-chan, tell me everything.

15:27.900 --> 15:29.300
How did the crisis start?

15:29.300 --> 15:30.200
What's going on now?

15:30.200 --> 15:30.690
Everything.

15:31.650 --> 15:33.520
It will take a while.

15:34.810 --> 15:36.600
<i>Damn it all!</i>

15:36.600 --> 15:41.120
<i>They won't let me use the One Order 
unless the vampire armies attack?!</i>

15:41.550 --> 15:42.830
<i>Very well.</i>

15:42.830 --> 15:44.540
<i>I'll give them exactly that.</i>

15:44.910 --> 15:46.800
<i>I'll start the battle!</i>

15:47.620 --> 15:53.690
<i>Eight amphibious assault vessels and 
60 rocket-equipped destroyers in the Pacific.</i>

15:53.690 --> 15:57.480
<i>High-altitude cruise missiles
 armed in their silos.</i>

15:57.480 --> 16:00.700
<i>Airborne troops landing 
throughout the entire world.</i>

16:00.700 --> 16:04.140
<i>A military deployment akin to a world war!</i>

16:04.560 --> 16:06.890
<i>I can pull the trigger oh so easily.</i>

16:07.200 --> 16:09.730
<i>All I need do is to wield Bram's holy sword.</i>

16:10.690 --> 16:11.570
Bram!

16:14.300 --> 16:15.660
He's gone!

16:15.660 --> 16:17.790
Bram's been stolen?!

16:19.140 --> 16:21.220
<i>What the hell am I doing?!</i>

16:21.220 --> 16:23.250
<i>I can't believe myself!</i>

16:23.620 --> 16:28.130
<i>Without Bram, I can't order the 
vampires of the world to march!</i>

16:28.130 --> 16:30.990
<i>The release of the One Order and 
the worldwide rewriting of reality</i>

16:30.990 --> 16:33.760
<i>using the back of the page become impossible!</i>

16:35.170 --> 16:38.470
Instruct the vampires to shut 
down all areas of the airport!

16:39.510 --> 16:42.350
<i>I suspect it was one of 
Jouno's men who stole him.</i>

16:42.670 --> 16:44.300
When you find the thief...

16:45.270 --> 16:46.580
Kill them!

16:48.730 --> 16:50.670
<i>I am Sigma...</i>

16:50.670 --> 16:52.100
<i>A man of the casino.</i>

16:52.860 --> 16:55.930
<i>I'm aware that I come from very special origins.</i>

16:56.490 --> 16:57.070
<i>Yet...</i>

16:57.740 --> 17:00.330
<i>I can't help but wonder...</i>

17:01.400 --> 17:04.370
So this'll causes death in half an hour, huh?

17:04.610 --> 17:05.700
Yup!

17:05.700 --> 17:08.120
You'll be bleeding from 
every orifice of your body.

17:08.120 --> 17:09.890
It's a work of art.

17:09.890 --> 17:13.160
<i>Am I the only sane person in this room?</i>

17:13.160 --> 17:15.040
The game's simple.

17:15.040 --> 17:17.990
Whoever escapes from Mersault first wins.

17:17.990 --> 17:20.920
I'll have the two of you 
take that injection.

17:20.920 --> 17:25.140
Only the first to escape 
will receive this antidote!

17:25.500 --> 17:26.350
Which means...

17:26.680 --> 17:30.560
In half an hour, 
either Dazai-kun or I will die.

17:30.920 --> 17:33.470
I must apologize to you, Dazai-kun.

17:34.250 --> 17:37.460
I'm really only interested 
in killing Fyodor-kun,

17:37.790 --> 17:41.440
but this is the only way I can 
get him to take the poison.

17:41.670 --> 17:43.390
Why apologize?

17:43.390 --> 17:45.150
This is a fantastic opportunity.

17:45.150 --> 17:46.400
A gift from heaven.

17:46.640 --> 17:48.120
Indeed.

17:48.120 --> 17:53.300
But it's also a little sad to think my 
chess buddy will be gone in half an hour.

17:53.750 --> 17:55.290
You're already sure you're going to win?

17:55.640 --> 17:57.870
What other conclusion could there be?

18:01.440 --> 18:05.420
<i>These guys laughed while 
taking a lethal injection.</i>

18:07.340 --> 18:11.770
It's time for the apostatic Nikolai Game!

18:12.530 --> 18:14.160
Let's begin.

18:15.560 --> 18:17.410
<i>Emergency announcement.</i>

18:17.410 --> 18:22.340
<i>A vehicle has caught fire 
at the Terminal 2 runway.</i>

18:22.670 --> 18:26.260
<i>For your safety, we are escorting 
all visitors outside the building.</i>

18:25.000 --> 18:26.260
Please line up single file.

18:26.520 --> 18:28.010
Please allow us to inspect your belongings.

18:28.290 --> 18:30.910
Shoot, everything's closed.

18:31.350 --> 18:32.210
Take me back.

18:32.590 --> 18:36.530
We could easily escape if only 
we can get out of the airport...

18:36.530 --> 18:38.120
Take me back to my coffin.

18:38.120 --> 18:38.970
I'm sleepy.

18:39.360 --> 18:42.210
Hey, Bra-chan, do something about them!

18:42.210 --> 18:45.640
You ask me to help you, a lowly thief?

18:45.640 --> 18:46.610
How laughable.

18:47.960 --> 18:49.010
I see.

18:49.300 --> 18:51.270
So that's how you're gonna be.

18:51.270 --> 18:54.470
Your attitude has become insolent.

18:56.760 --> 18:57.500
It won't come out.

18:57.500 --> 18:59.190
How dare you! You fool!

18:59.560 --> 19:01.190
This sword will not come out!

19:01.190 --> 19:04.430
It's embedded in my brain!

19:04.890 --> 19:06.030
Meaning?

19:06.030 --> 19:08.450
It hurts a lot when you pull on it.

19:08.450 --> 19:11.960
But we have to do something,
or there's going to be worldwide war!

19:11.960 --> 19:13.680
We have to do something!

19:13.680 --> 19:15.520
A foolish girl you are.

19:15.520 --> 19:17.590
I am the archduke of darkness.

19:17.590 --> 19:20.350
King of demons, enemy of man.

19:22.450 --> 19:24.180
You're right.

19:24.180 --> 19:26.990
You're talking to a complete idiot.

19:27.570 --> 19:29.510
To prove it, look at this.

19:31.740 --> 19:34.120
I can't stop shaking.

19:35.600 --> 19:37.230
I don't have anything.

19:37.630 --> 19:40.180
No special abilities,
no knowledge, no strength.

19:41.350 --> 19:44.380
All I have is the determination

19:44.380 --> 19:47.760
I've built up over ten years,
to never run away in this kind of crisis.

19:48.780 --> 19:50.710
You are ten years of age?

19:51.290 --> 19:54.630
Not even old enough to use a loom.

19:55.280 --> 19:58.350
Why does such a girl fight?

19:58.760 --> 20:00.190
Why?

20:02.370 --> 20:03.290
No!

20:03.860 --> 20:06.840
Wrap the rag around your fingers!

20:06.840 --> 20:09.400
Don't step on the edge of 
the tatami when you scrub.

20:09.790 --> 20:11.840
The water bucket is to be three-fifths full.

20:12.140 --> 20:16.410
Your mother could clean, cook,
 sew, manage the finances...

20:16.410 --> 20:19.430
She could do everything. 
She was the perfect woman.

20:19.430 --> 20:21.100
Okay, but justice is my—

20:21.100 --> 20:25.750
You're a failure of a woman!

20:29.830 --> 20:33.560
So, Bra-chan, all I've got is determination.

20:34.020 --> 20:37.250
That's why I need help from 
the people of that world.

20:37.880 --> 20:39.650
Okay? Please?

20:39.650 --> 20:41.000
I'll do anything in return.

20:41.370 --> 20:42.370
In return?

20:43.480 --> 20:47.310
There's little a commoner could offer.

20:54.680 --> 20:58.440
You most certainly could 
not offer me this...

20:58.440 --> 21:01.640
but there is one treasure I desire.

21:02.360 --> 21:03.440
What?!

21:03.700 --> 21:07.660
The ultimate mechanical orchestra, 
of which I hear rumors...

21:07.660 --> 21:12.400
The legendary treasure, containing 
musicians in a box the size of a fist...

21:15.660 --> 21:17.600
The wireless radio!

21:19.400 --> 21:20.360
Huh?

21:19.400 --> 21:20.360
Huh?

21:20.330 --> 21:25.530
It shall soothe me in my long 
slumber within the coffin.

21:25.530 --> 21:31.300
Provide me with this treasure,
and I shall be glad to offer you my flesh.

21:31.570 --> 21:33.310
A r-radio?

21:33.920 --> 21:35.040
See?

21:35.040 --> 21:36.400
You cannot, can you?

21:36.400 --> 21:37.820
A radio...

21:37.820 --> 21:40.130
Did my dad use one before?

21:40.130 --> 21:41.870
No, but...

21:42.780 --> 21:44.160
Will this do?

21:46.610 --> 21:50.330
<b>Kiseki</b>

21:50.320 --> 21:52.870
I've got 200 online channels.

21:52.870 --> 21:55.530
And you can find just about 
any music if you pay for it.

22:00.510 --> 22:01.950
I may have this?

22:01.950 --> 22:03.000
Yeah.

22:03.000 --> 22:03.970
It's yours.

22:09.410 --> 22:12.190
Are you a goddess?

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode
Episode 57

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
<i>At the Port in the Sky (Part 3)</i>
